From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 09:42:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 046/184] segacd: make the command counter wrap, because
 saturated is not alive

It saturated at 255 and was displayed masked to three bits. 255 masked
to three bits is 7, so about three seconds after boot the counter
parked on 7 and stayed there -- and I read that constant as proof the
interrupt was still running, for several builds after it had stopped.

A liveness counter that stops counting is not a liveness counter.
---
 bios/segacd.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index 0d66577..66b9213 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -144,7 +144,12 @@ static UBYTE cdd_next[9];       /* built by the VBL, taken by level 4 */
 static ULONG cdd_outbuf[3];     /* aligned: the write below is long-wide */
 #define cdd_out ((UBYTE *)cdd_outbuf)
 static UBYTE cdd_handover;
-static UBYTE cdd_sent;          /* commands actually handed to the drive */
+static UBYTE cdd_sent;          /* commands handed to the drive. Wraps, and
+                                 * must: it used to saturate at 255, and 255
+                                 * masked to three bits is a constant 7 -- so
+                                 * the counter parked after three seconds and
+                                 * was read as proof of life for several
+                                 * builds after the interrupt had stopped */
 static UBYTE cdd_irqs;          /* level-4 arrivals, for the watchdog */
 static UBYTE cdd_seen;          /* last count the watchdog looked at */
 static UBYTE cdd_quiet;         /* VBLs since the interrupt last fired */
